"""Optimize fixed-tilt PV design for Hornsund using the existing PV capacity-factor model.

DESIGN VARIABLES OPTIMIZED
--------------------------
1) Surface tilt beta [deg]
2) Surface azimuth gamma [deg]

Azimuth convention is inherited from the Hornsund PV model:
    0 deg   = South
   -90 deg  = East
   +90 deg  = West
 +/-180 deg = North

OBJECTIVE
---------
Maximize annual specific PV production [kWh/kWp]. For a fixed annual number of
hours this is equivalent to maximizing mean annual capacity factor.

MODEL COUPLING
--------------
This optimizer dynamically imports the user's existing Hornsund PV script and
reuses its:
- irradiation reader and GHI/DHI/BHI interpretation;
- 3-hourly -> hourly conversion;
- SEKLIMA temperature alignment;
- solar-position convention;
- 2015 Hornsund/Fuglebekken snow-cover-based rho(t);
- NOCT temperature correction;
- derating, clipping, BHI/DNI interpretation and numerical safeguards.

The optimizer does NOT optimize ALBEDO_MIN, ALBEDO_MAX, derating, NOCT,
temperature coefficient, etc. Those are model/environmental parameters, not PV
orientation design variables. It reads them from the selected base PV script.

The search uses a coarse grid over the requested ranges, followed by a finer
local grid around the best coarse point. Results are therefore grid-optimal at
the selected fine resolution, not an analytical continuous optimum.
"""

from __future__ import annotations

